      "In 1995 Kwiat, Weinfurter, Herzog, Zeilinger, and Kasevich used the Zeno effect to raise the efficiency of interaction-free measurement toward 100 percent. In 2002 Childs and coauthors described Quantum Search by Measurement, an algorithm that finds a marked item by repeatedly measuring a system, in the spirit of adiabatic evolution. Facchi and Pascazio introduced Zeno subspaces in 2002, and Franson, Jacobs, and Pittman proposed Zeno-based photonic gates in 2004. Counterfactual communication protocols based on the effect were proposed by Salih and coauthors in 2013, with an experimental demonstration by a Chinese group in 2017.",
