      "Quantum belief propagation carries the idea over to quantum systems, where the variables are quantum and the probabilities become density matrices. It is mostly an algorithm run on classical computers to study quantum states, and it also shows up in the decoding of quantum error-correcting codes. It is not a quantum speedup in itself.",
