      "Poulin and Bilgin applied the method in 2008 to compute correlation functions of quantum systems on loopy graphs. In parallel, belief propagation became a practical tool for quantum error correction: Panteleev and Kalachev and Roffe and colleagues showed around 2020 and 2021 that decoders combining belief propagation with ordered statistics post-processing work well for quantum LDPC codes, and similar decoders have been developed for hardware roadmaps by groups such as IBM.",
