      "The quantum case adds a difficulty. Quantum operators on neighboring pieces generally do not commute, so the neat factorization of probabilities no longer holds. Leifer and Poulin replaced the factorization with a notion of quantum conditional independence defined through the quantum conditional mutual information, which vanishes for states with the structure of a quantum Markov chain. For such states, local quantum messages can be defined and passed in the same way.",
      "On trees this gives exact marginals under the right structural assumptions, and on loopy graphs it gives approximations whose quality depends on correlations decaying with distance. Hastings's version uses a similar message structure to correct the errors that arise when a thermal state is approximated by local pieces.",
