      "Quantum natural gradient corrects for that. It measures steps by how much the quantum state changes, not by how much the angles change, using the Fubini-Study metric tensor, which is a quantum version of the Fisher information matrix. The method often converges in fewer iterations than ordinary gradient descent, at the price of extra circuit evaluations to estimate the metric.",
