      "Quantum Gibbs sampling is the task of preparing such a state, or sampling from it, efficiently. It is a fundamental problem in quantum algorithms and in physics. At low temperatures it is as hard as finding the ground state, so no general efficient algorithm exists. Recent theoretical breakthroughs have given rigorous efficient algorithms at high temperatures and new, better-behaved quantum analogues of classical Markov chain methods.",
