      "A key theoretical development was Brandão and Kastoryano's 2019 result that finite correlation length implies efficient preparation of thermal states. In 2023, Chen, Kastoryano, Brandão, and Gilyén introduced a quantum thermal state preparation method based on a Lindbladian that approximately satisfies detailed balance, and Chen, Kastoryano, and Gilyén followed with an exact version. In 2024, Rouzé, França, and Alhambra, and separately Bakshi, Liu, Moitra, and Tang, proved efficiency at high temperatures. Gilyén, Chen, Doriguello, and Kastoryano developed quantum generalizations of Glauber and Metropolis dynamics the same year.",
